('ANIME', 'Into the Forest of Fireflies'' Light', 'Hotarubi no Mori e', '蛍火の杜へ', 'The story of Hotarubi no Mori e centers around Hotaru, a little girl who gets lost in an enchanted forest where apparitions reside. A young boy, Gin, appears before Hotaru, but she cannot touch him for fear of making him disappear.', '{"Drama","Fantasy","Romance","Supernatural"}', '{"coming-of-age","youkai","rural","urban-fantasy","male-protagonist","shoujo","female-protagonist","heterosexual","iyashikei","wilderness"}', '1', NULL, NULL, '45', '2011', 'SUMMER', 'MOVIE', 'FINISHED', 196159, '79', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/media/anime/cover/large/bx10408-PlKJ6DAyvMk2.png', 'https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/media/anime/banner/10408-kZhXe0uVrAd2.jpg', '#93d678', 10408, '10408', '{"Brain''s Base"}', '[{"url": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/media/anime/banner/10408-kZhXe0uVrAd2.jpg", "kind": "banner", "caption": "Key visual"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/qXLSRH31Yao/hqdefault.jpg", "kind": "trailer", "caption": "Trailer", "video": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qXLSRH31Yao"}]'::jsonb, '[{"name": "Gin", "native": "ギン", "role": "MAIN", "image": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b41311-QbW9aecoguFX.png"}, {"name": "Hotaru Takegawa", "native": "竹川蛍", "role": "MAIN", "image": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b41371-bgilENMWqYZN.png"}, {"name": "Haha", "native": "母", "role": "SUPPORTING", "image": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b60689-Gyob1nbPwvGv.png"}, {"name": "Ryouta", "native": "亮太", "role": "SUPPORTING", "image": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b60691-ZLXknNFcU2Uz.png"}, {"name": "Sofu", "native": "祖父", "role": "SUPPORTING", "image": "https://s4.anilist.co/file/anilistcdn/character/large/b274039-BByjG8feeZeR.jpg"}]'::jsonb, 'anilist', '10408'),
('ANIME', 'MUSHI-SHI', 'Mushishi', '蟲師', 'Neither good nor evil, they are life in its purest form. Vulgar and strange, they have inspired fear in humans since the dawn of time and have, over the ages, come to be known as "mushi." The stories of the Mushi and the people they affect are all linked together by a traveling Mushi-shi, or "Mushi Master," who seeks rare Mushi sightings and uses his shaman-like knowledge of Mushi to help the affected people.

